## Original Content
With 5,514 confirmed cases and 2,642 deaths, the World Health Organization warns this is now the nation's fastest-growing outbreak to date.

## Summary
The Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of the Congo has reached 5,514 confirmed cases and 2,642 deaths. The World Health Organization warns that this is the fastest-growing outbreak in the country's history, highlighting its rapid spread and severity.

## Key Points
- 5,514 confirmed cases of Ebola reported in DR Congo
- 2,642 deaths attributed to the outbreak
- World Health Organization has issued a warning about the outbreak
- This is described as the fastest-growing outbreak in the nation's history


